# The Power of Cyberlearning: An Empirical Test.

**Authors:** Navarro, Peter, Shoemaker, Judy

## Abstract
This study of graduate students in business in a required introductory macroeconomics course compared the effectiveness of cyberlearning and traditional classroom instruction. Students identified themselves as either cyberlearners (n=32) or traditional learners (n=31). Cyberlearners used CD-ROMs, online quizzes, and discussions. Comparison of academic outcomes found no significant differences on six of eight academic variables. (DB)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ613256

